Use for travel plans, todos, notes the user asked to keep. Prefer structured Markdown (headings, lists).
For the sidebar calendar "memo dot", include a date like YYYY-MM-DD in section_title or in the first lines of content (or use default append heading which includes the date).
mode "append" adds a new dated section; "replace" overwrites the whole memo (use only when the user explicitly wants to clear or replace everything).
Args JSON: {"content": "...", "mode": "append"|"replace", "section_title": "optional heading for append"} name:memo_write parameters:map[properties:map[content:map[description:Markdown text to save. type:string] mode:map[description:append (default): add a section; replace: overwrite entire memo. enum:[append replace] type:string] section_title:map[description:Optional section heading when mode is append; default is local date-time. type:string]] required:[content] type:object] results:map[description:Confirmation with memo file path. type:string]] map[description:
Query financial market data and generate structured analysis.

Use this tool when:
- The user asks about stock market, crypto, or financial markets
- The query involves price, trend, or investment conditions
- The user asks about "today market", "market situation", "price movement"

You MUST use this tool instead of general search when the question is about financial markets.

This tool provides structured insights including:
- Trend analysis
- Volatility
- Risk level
- Market sentiment

Valid symbol examples:
- Stocks: AAPL, MSFT, GOOGL, TSLA
- Crypto: BTC-USD, ETH-USD
- Indices: ^GSPC (S&P 500), ^DJI (Dow Jones)

IMPORTANT: Always provide a valid market symbol in the 'symbol' parameter.
If user doesn't specify a symbol, use a default like 'AAPL' or ask the user.

Do NOT rely on search tools for market data if this tool is available.
 name:query_market parameters:map[properties:map[symbol:map[description:Market symbol (e.g., AAPL, BTC-USD, ^GSPC) type:string]] required:[symbol] type:object] results:map[description:Structured market data analysis including price, trend, volatility, and insights properties:map[analysis:map[description:Market analysis and indicators properties:map[liquidity:map[description:Market liquidity (low, normal, high) example:normal type:string] market_sentiment:map[description:Overall market sentiment (bullish, bearish, neutral) example:bullish type:string] risk_level:map[description:Risk level (low, medium, high) example:low type:string]] type:object] insights:map[description:Key market insights and observations example:[Market is in uptrend phase Volatility is low] items:map[type:string] type:array] summary:map[description:Summary of market data properties:map[change:map[description:Price change from previous close example:%!s(float64=0.5) type:number] change_percent:map[description:Percentage change from previous close example:0.33% type:string] current_price:map[description:Current market price example:%!s(float64=150.25) type:number] open:map[description:Opening price for the current period example:%!s(float64=148.5) type:number] previous_close:map[description:Previous closing price example:%!s(float64=149.75) type:number] trend:map[description:Market trend (uptrend, downtrend, sideways) example:uptrend type:string] volatility:map[description:Volatility level (low, medium, high) example:low type:string] volume:map[description:Trading volume example:%!s(int=1000000) type:integer] volume_trend:map[description:Volume trend (stable, increasing, decreasing) example:stable type:string]] type:object] symbol:map[description:Market symbol (e.g., AAPL, BTC-USD) example:AAPL type:string] timestamp:map[description:Timestamp of the data in RFC3339 format example:2024-01-15T10:30:00Z type:string]] type:object]] map[description:传入date获取date对应日期和时间的详细信息，只要问今天适合干什么，问今天的运势，只要关于运气，玄学等等关于气运的都要调用这个接口。
	支持星座、儒略日、干支、生肖、节气、节日、彭祖百忌、吉神(喜神/福神/财神/阳贵神/阴贵神)方位、胎神方位、冲煞、纳音、星宿、八字、五行、十神、建除十二值星、青龙名堂等十二神、黄道日及吉凶、法定节假日及调休等,about almanac name:get_date_info_about_almanac parameters:map[properties:map[date:map[description:必要参数，指定查询的日期，格式为'YYYY-MM-DD'，如'2023-01-01'，或者不指定，则默认为当前时间 type:string]] required:[date] type:object] results:map[description:Comprehensive date information including solar and lunar calendar details, zodiac, festivals, and traditional almanac data properties:map[almanac:map[description:Traditional Chinese almanac information example:甲辰年 丁丑月 戊子日 (冲马 煞南) type:string] current_time:map[description:Current date and time in format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' example:2024-01-15 10:30:45 type:string] day_gan_zhi:map[description:Gan-Zhi (Stem-Branch) representation of the day example:戊子 type:string] holiday:map[description:Holiday information (only present if it's a holiday) example:春节 type:string] lunar_date:map[description:Lunar calendar date in Chinese format example:甲辰年腊月初五 type:string] month_gan_zhi:map[description:Gan-Zhi (Stem-Branch) representation of the month example:丁丑 type:string] solar_term:map[description:Solar term information (if applicable) example:小寒 type:string] weekday:map[description:Day of the week in Chinese example:星期一 type:string] year_gan_zhi:map[description:Gan-Zhi (Stem-Branch) representation of the year example:甲辰 type:string] zodiac:map[description:Chinese zodiac animal for the year example:龙 type:string]] type:object]] map[description:Calculates time by adding or subtracting duration from current time. Args format: 'operation:duration' where operation is 'add' or 'subtract', and duration is like '1h30m' (hours and minutes) name:calculate_time parameters:map[properties:map[duration:map[description:The duration to add or subtract, e.g., '1h30m' for 1 hour and 30 minutes type:string] operation:map[description:The operation to perform: 'add' or 'subtract' type:string]] required:[operation duration] type:object] results:map[description:Calculated time result properties:map[calculated_time:map[description:The calculated time in RFC3339 format example:2024-01-15T10:30:00+08:00 type:string]] type:object]] map[description:Tool for executing local bash (Linux/Mac) or cmd (Windows) commands. Use this tool when user needs to run system commands, check system status, or perform local operations. Returns command output, error messages, and exit code. 当用户需要执行系统命令、根据软件运行的系统类型，选择对应的系统命令。使用这个工具时，务必确保输入的命令是安全的，并且不会对系统造成破坏。系统的类型是:windows name:execute_command parameters:map[properties:map[command:map[description:The command to execute type:string]] required:[command] type:object] results:map[description:Execution results of the command including output, error messages, and exit code properties:map[command:map[description:The command that was executed example:ls -la type:string] error:map[description:Error message if the command failed (only present if there was an error) example:exit status 127 type:string] exit_code:map[description:Exit code of the command (only present if the command failed) example:%!s(int=127) type:integer] output:map[description:Standard output and error from the command example:total 24
drwxr-xr-x 5 user group 4096 Jan 15 10:30 . type:string] success:map[description:Whether the command executed successfully example:%!s(bool=true) type:boolean]] type:object]] map[description:Manage files and folders inside the app's document library root (a folder named "workspace" under the app working directory). All paths are relative to that root — use forward slashes (e.g. "小说/三侠五义/第一回.md"). Safe: cannot escape outside the library.

Use for: creating novel/project folders, chapter files, notes trees. Combine with operation write_file for content. Prefer mkdir before write_file when the parent folder does not exist.

Operations:
- list_dir: list entries in "path" (default "").
- mkdir: create directory "path" (and parents).
- write_file: overwrite file at "path" with "content" (UTF-8 text).
- delete: remove file or empty directory; set recursive_delete true to remove a non-empty directory tree.
- rename: move/rename from "path" to "path_to".

Example: user wants 小说/三侠五义 with chapters — mkdir "小说", mkdir "小说/三侠五义", write_file "小说/三侠五义/第一回.md" with content, etc. name:library_fs parameters:map[properties:map[content:map[description:For write_file: full file content (overwrite). type:string] operation:map[description:Action to perform. enum:[list_dir mkdir write_file delete rename] type:string] path:map[description:Relative path inside the library (e.g. 小说/三侠五义). Use "" for list_dir root. type:string] path_to:map[description:For rename: new relative path inside the library. type:string] recursive_delete:map[description:For delete: if true, remove directories with all contents. Default false. type:boolean]] required:[operation] type:object] results:map[description:Result message or JSON (list_dir). type:string]] map[description:Write or continue long-form fiction under workspace/: chapter_XX[_标题slug].md (slug from model chapter_title), rolling novel_bible.md, per-chapter JSON under meta/, author_log.md, and reader_milestones.md every 10 chapters.
Use the same output_dir + resume=true to continue tomorrow with new ideas (author_notes). premise each time can restate direction plus new beats.
Parameters: premise (required), outline (optional), chapter_count (chapters to write this run, 1–30, default 6), output_dir (default novels/story_<unix>), resume (continue existing folder), author_notes (new ideas this session), refresh_outline (regenerate outline when resuming), style, language. name:novel_longform parameters:map[properties:map[author_notes:map[description:Optional: new ideas, tone shifts, or reminders for this session; appended to author_log.md with timestamp. type:string] chapter_count:map[description:Chapters to write in this invocation (1–30). Default 6. On resume, adds this many chapters after the last existing file. type:integer] language:map[description:Optional language name (e.g. 简体中文). If omitted, follow the premise language. type:string] outline:map[description:Optional outline. If empty on a new project, the tool generates one. On resume, existing outline.md is kept unless refresh_outline is true. type:string] output_dir:map[description:Directory under workspace/ (relative, no ..). Default: novels/story_<timestamp>. Reuse for continuation. type:string] premise:map[description:Story direction: first run = core idea; resume = today's continuation goals plus any new beats (keep concise). type:string] refresh_outline:map[description:If true with resume, regenerates outline from premise (overwrites outline.md). Use sparingly. type:boolean] resume:map[description:If true, continue from the last chapter_*.md in output_dir; load bible and meta/*.json. Same folder as a writer's project. type:boolean] style:map[description:Optional narrative style (e.g. literary, light novel, suspense). type:string]] required:[premise] type:object] results:map[description:JSON string: output_dir, files written, chapters_written, chapter_range, resume_used. type:object]] map[description:Tool for getting the current real-time date and time from the server. MUST use this tool when user asks about current time, today's date, or any time-related questions requiring real-time information. Returns date, time, weekday, lunar date, and holiday information.只要对话里涉及时间的要应该先调用这个接口获取当前时间，再根据用户需求进行回复 name:get_current_time parameters:map[properties:map[] required:[] type:object] results:map[description:Current time information including date, weekday, lunar date, and holiday properties:map[current_time:map[description:Current date and time in format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' example:2024-01-15 10:30:45 type:string] holiday:map[description:Holiday information (only present if it's a holiday) example:春节 type:string] lunar_date:map[description:Chinese lunar calendar date example:腊月初五 type:string] weekday:map[description:Day of the week in Chinese example:星期一 type:string]] type:object]] map[description:Converts a location name (city, address, landmark) into latitude and longitude coordinates. Input should be a place name like 'Beijing', 'New York', or 'Eiffel Tower'. Returns the coordinates and additional location details. name:geocoding parameters:map[properties:map[location:map[description:The location name to geocode. Must use 'location' as the parameter name. Examples: 'Beijing', 'Times Square', 'Tokyo Tower' type:string]] required:[location] type:object] results:map[description:Geocoding tool to convert a location name into latitude and longitude coordinates properties:map[latitude:map[description:The latitude coordinate of the location example:39.9042 type:string] longitude:map[description:The longitude coordinate of the location example:116.4074 type:string]] type:object]] map[description:Get weather and forecast information for a specific location. This tool provides comprehensive weather data including temperature, humidity, wind speed, precipitation probability, and weather conditions. Use this tool when user asks about weather, temperature, or forecast for any location. Requires latitude and longitude coordinates of the location. name:query_weather parameters:map[properties:map[days:map[description:Number of days to forecast (default: 7, max: 16) type:integer] latitude:map[description:The latitude coordinate of the location (e.g., 39.9042 for Beijing) type:string] longitude:map[description:The longitude coordinate of the location (e.g., 116.4074 for Beijing) type:string]] required:[latitude longitude] type:object] results:map[description:Weather forecast data with daily breakdown and insights properties:map[daily_forecast:map[description:Array of daily weather forecasts items:map[properties:map[date:map[description:Date in YYYY-MM-DD format example:2024-01-15 type:string] insights:map[description:Daily weather insights and recommendations example:[Temperature rising High chance of rain - consider carrying an umbrella] items:map[type:string] type:array] summary:map[properties:map[condition:map[description:Primary weather condition example:Partly cloudy type:string] max_precip_prob:map[description:Maximum precipitation probability (0-100) example:%!s(int=30) type:integer] max_wind_speed:map[description:Maximum wind speed in km/h example:%!s(float64=15.5) type:number] temperature_range:map[description:Temperature range in Celsius example:15.5°C ~ 22.3°C type:string] trend:map[description:Temperature trend (warming/cooling/stable) example:warming type:string]] type:object]] type:object] type:array] forecast_days:map[description:Number of days in the forecast (1-16) example:%!s(int=3) type:integer] overall_insights:map[description:Overall weather trends and patterns for the forecast period example:[Overall temperature trend: Warming up over the forecast period Rain expected on 2 day(s) during the forecast period] items:map[type:string] type:array]] type:object]] map[description:
	Writes a chunk of content to a file at a specific offset.
	
	This tool is designed for writing large files that exceed the token limit.
	You should break down large content into smaller chunks and call this tool
	multiple times, each with a different offset.
	
	IMPORTANT: 
	- The first call should have offset = 0
	- Subsequent calls should have offset equal to total size of previously written content
	- The last chunk should have is_last = true
	- If is_last is true, file will be truncated at current offset + content length
	- CRITICAL: Each chunk must not exceed 100 characters to ensure reliable processing
	
	To use this tool:
	1. Provide the actual filename, content, offset, and is_last values
	2. Do NOT provide the parameter schema/definition
	3. Call this tool multiple times for large files, each time with the next offset
	
	Args (example values):
	{
	  "filename": "large_file.txt",
	  "content": "First part of the content...",
	  "offset": 0,
	  "is_last": false
	}
	
	Example usage for writing a large file:
	1. First chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "First part of the content...",
	     "offset": 0,
	     "is_last": false
	   })
	   
	2. Second chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "Second part of the content...",
	     "offset": 1024,
	     "is_last": false
	   })
	   
	3. Last chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "Last part of the content...",
	     "offset": 2048,
	     "is_last": true
	   })
	   
	Note: When writing large files, ensure each chunk is within the 100 character limit
	for reliable processing. If a chunk exceeds this limit, it may be truncated or fail.
	 name:write_file_chunk parameters:map[properties:map[content:map[description:The content chunk to write to the file. type:string] filename:map[description:The path to the file. Can be an absolute path or a relative path. type:string] is_last:map[description:True if this is the last chunk, false otherwise. type:boolean] offset:map[description:The byte offset in the file where this chunk should be written. type:integer]] required:[filename content offset is_last] type:object] results:map[description:Result of the file write operation properties:map[bytes_written:map[description:Number of bytes written in this chunk example:%!s(int=1024) type:integer] filename:map[description:The absolute path of the file that was written to example:/path/to/large_file.txt type:string] is_last:map[description:Indicates whether this was the last chunk to write example:%!s(bool=false) type:boolean] offset:map[description:The offset in the file where the chunk was written example:%!s(int=0) type:integer] success:map[description:Indicates whether the write operation was successful example:%!s(bool=true) type:boolean]] type:object]]]
